From: Jeremy Selan <jeremys@valvesoftware.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Apr 2024 17:19:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] disable security check on grantRuntimePermission

This allows all permissions to be settable via command-line (or API), even those that
traditionally require user intervention like MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE.

Change-Id: I51a2268611b6c8125ffd986fb78b38bf51f3d99f
---
 .../java/com/android/server/pm/permission/BasePermission.java   | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/permission/BasePermission.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/permission/BasePermission.java
index 354f5b9a8bd..dc22b6e98a1 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/permission/BasePermission.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/permission/BasePermission.java
@@ -442,6 +442,7 @@ public final class BasePermission {
 
     public void enforceDeclaredUsedAndRuntimeOrDevelopment(AndroidPackage pkg,
             PackageSetting pkgSetting) {
+        /*
         final PermissionsState permsState = pkgSetting.getPermissionsState();
         int index = pkg.getRequestedPermissions().indexOf(name);
         if (!permsState.hasRequestedPermission(name) && index == -1) {
@@ -452,6 +453,7 @@ public final class BasePermission {
             throw new SecurityException("Permission " + name + " requested by "
                     + pkg.getPackageName() + " is not a changeable permission type");
         }
+        */
     }
 
     private static BasePermission findPermissionTree(
